<!--
  Copy this file to "secrets.props" beside it and put your own key in.

  secrets.props is gitignored, so it never reaches the repository. It is read automatically by
  every build, which is the same thing Prism does with theirs: the key belongs to whoever owns
  the application, and is compiled into that owner's releases rather than committed.

  Get a key at https://console.curseforge.com/?#/api-keys — it is free.

  Use your own. A key is issued to one application, and CurseForge's terms require a derivative
  work to obtain its own rather than reuse the one it was forked with. The same line appears
  beside Prism's key, for the same reason.

  Without it, Modrinth still works everywhere. Only the CurseForge source stays switched off.
-->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <CurseForgeApiKey>PUT_YOUR_KEY_HERE</CurseForgeApiKey>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
